          "key": "unsafe_code",
          "lead": [
            "# NO UNSAFE, and it is FORBID rather than deny: this crate parses hostile-shaped text off the",
            "# network into a verdict, so nothing in it has any business reaching for a raw pointer, and",
            "# `forbid` cannot be lifted by an `#[allow]` further in. It lived as `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` in",
            "# `src/lib.rs` until that file stopped existing (`a-crate-root-is-shared-so-a-crate-is-one-file`):",
            "# the crate root is SHARED by every adopter now, so a per-crate inner attribute has nowhere to sit",
            "# and the manifest — a file that stays regardless — is where cargo has read this since 1.74."
          ],
          "value": "\"forbid\""
